  "identifier": "ptb-xl",
  "name": "PTB-XL",
  "alternateName": [
    "PTB-XL ECG Dataset"
  ],
  "description": "Large publicly available 12-lead ECG dataset containing 21,799 clinical recordings from 18,869 patients (ages 0–95, 52% male) collected at the Physikalisch-Technische Bundesanstalt (PTB). Each record is a 10-second 12-lead ECG annotated by up to two cardiologists with 71 standardised SCP-ECG diagnostic, form, and rhythm statements. Provided in WFDB format at two sampling frequencies: 500 Hz (full) and 100 Hz (downsampled). Includes signal quality metadata (noise, baseline drift, artefacts) and comprehensive demographic and clinical metadata. Supplies recommended train/validation/test splits for reproducible benchmarking. CC BY 4.0, v1.0.3 (November 2022). Published in Scientific Data 2020 (Wagner et al.). The de facto benchmark for deep learning ECG classification research.",
  "url": "https://physionet.org/content/ptb-xl/",
  "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
  "version": "1.0.3",
  "dateModified": "2022-11-09",
